 "corner_construction": {
  "method": "Q-A ruling: measured worst-case direction, not hand-declared loadings",
  "steps": [
   "1. Calibrate U0 per group (see _U0_calibration).",
   "2. Measure g_i = d ln(metric)/d z_i for every variable the group depends on, on its classic bench.",
   "3. z_fast = 3 * g / |g|; z_slow = -z_fast. Mahalanobis length is exactly 3 by construction.",
   "4. Record bench, bias, and the g vector (classic and analog) in corners.json."
  ],
  "shared_variable_rule": "When several selected groups pull a shared variable the same way, the preset generator takes the normalized sum of directions and rescales to the preset's declared distance. Conflicts are reported in corners.json; last-listed group wins only in case = -1 manual mode.",
  "SPD_note": "SPD_<group> is a derived direction, not a sampled variable. Monte Carlo samples the independent variables; SPD exists only to define corners."
 },
